.TH NWSTOP 1 "October 2026" "nwstop 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nwstop \- network traffic monitor for VPN nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nwstop
[\fB\-i\fR \fIIFACE\fR] [\fB\-\-vpn\-ports\fR \fIPORTS\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-dns\fR] [\fB\-\-mouse\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nwstop
captures packets on a network interface and shows, per remote IP address,
the service name, port, current rates and total transferred bytes.
It must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-iface " " \fIIFACE\fR
Interface to monitor. Defaults to the interface of the default route.
.TP
.BI \-\-vpn\-ports " PORTS"
Comma-separated local ports on which clients connect. Default: 443.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dns
Do not resolve reverse DNS names.
.TP
.B \-\-mouse
Enable mouse wheel scrolling.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR j ", " k ", arrows, PgUp, PgDn, g, G"
Scroll.
.TP
.BR 1 \- 4
Sort by 2s rate, 10s rate, 40s rate, total bytes.
.TP
.B c
Show only VPN clients.
.TP
.B /
Filter by IP, host or service.
.TP
.B p
Pause.
.TP
.B n
Toggle reverse DNS.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH AUTHOR
DarkRezet <darkrezet.music@gmail.com>
